lemma[fact] L32:argument-unidentified-man-hazardous-freight-siding-location-moving "The argument with an unidentified man, hazardous freight-siding location, moving wagons, severe short-sightedness, and stored spectacles collectively make deliberate luring or endangerment substantially more plausible than the preliminary accidental-death finding, without establishing the precise killing act."
  <- AND#J32(P20, P124, P125, P127, P128, P129, P130)

lemma[fact] L33:burned-row-17-fragment-ruth-spoken-distinction-between "The burned 'ROW—17' fragment, Ruth's spoken distinction between a row and an account, and her notebook entry strongly identify collection Row 17—and therefore the Vesper Psalter—as the referent of 'ROW 17'."
  <- AND#J33(P48, P126, P133, P134)

lemma[fact] L34:ruth-notebook-impressions-miriam-later-examination-independently-point "Ruth's notebook impressions and Miriam's later examination independently point toward modern blue paper fibers in the Vesper Psalter, though the notebook's intended meaning and Miriam's analysis still require appropriate evidentiary caution."
  <- AND#J34(P3, P133, P134, P136)

lemma[fact] L35:vesper-psalter-now-leading-candidate-aldous-alleged-false "The Vesper Psalter is now the leading candidate for Aldous's alleged false collection object, but Beatrice's restoration explanation remains an unverified alternative to wholesale forgery."
  <- AND#J35(P22, L33, L34, P138)

lemma[fact] L36:aldous-unfinished-sentence-consistent-someone-having-mistaken-ruth "Aldous's unfinished sentence is consistent with someone having mistaken Ruth's reference to collection Row 17 for a numbered account, but the missing completion prevents treating that reconstruction as certain."
