undercut[fact] CP5:chemical-examination-found-aconitine-both-concealed-needle-aldous ::T "Chemical examination found aconitine both on the concealed needle and in Aldous's body, superseding the earlier chemically unconfirmed diagnosis." -> inference J11:target L11

undercut[fact] CP6:watchmaker-identified-freshly-bent-balance-staff-showed-that ::T "The watchmaker identified a freshly bent balance staff and showed that a sideways desk jolt could stop the intact clock, resolving the previously unexplained mechanical context." -> inference J4:target L4

undercut[fact] CP7:estate-office-key-register-establishes-that-gideon-received ::T "The estate-office key register establishes that Gideon received the duplicate poison-cabinet key and that no return was recorded, superseding reliance on the earlier report that it was simply lost." -> inference J25:target L25

undercut[fact] CP8:professional-examination-independently-confirmed-retracting-needle ::T "Professional examination independently confirmed the retracting-needle mechanism, so identification of the design no longer depends materially on Cassian's testimony." -> inference J26:target L26

lemma[fact] L53:book-clasp-was-demonstrated-puncture-mechanism-pressing-it "The book clasp was the demonstrated puncture mechanism: pressing it projected an aconitine-bearing, dye-marked needle and releasing it concealed the needle inside the hollow spine."
  <- AND#J54(P182, P183, P184)

lemma[fact] L54:aldous-was-poisoned-aconitine-delivered-book-concealed-needle "Aldous was poisoned with aconitine delivered by the book's concealed needle; the matching dye explains the marked thumb puncture."
  <- AND#J55(P38, P184, P185)

lemma[fact] L55:vellum-book-was-recently-constructed-disguise-hollow-spine "The vellum book was a recently constructed disguise for the hollow-spine weapon: old opening leaves supplied plausibility, while the unread modern block supplied concealing thickness."
  <- AND#J56(P186, P187, P188, P189)

lemma[fact] L56:weapon-was-assembled-october-17-after-gideon-learned "The weapon was assembled by October 17, after Gideon learned that Aldous intended to expose Escrow 17 and before the October 18 dinner announcement."
  <- AND#J57(P178, P180, P190, P191)

lemma[fact] L57:gideon-had-documented-unreturned-custody-duplicate-poison-cabinet "Gideon had documented, unreturned custody of the duplicate poison-cabinet key, giving him a non-forced means of obtaining the missing aconitine; the register proves access rather than the act of removal by itself."
  <- AND#J58(P96, P102, P194, P195, P196)

lemma[fact] L58:gideon-encountered-ruth-her-open-notebook-while-she "Gideon encountered Ruth at her open notebook while she was investigating Row 17 and admits seeing at least that heading; he also uniquely among the other guests was shown to know of Escrow 17 before her death."
  <- AND#J59(P166, P197, P198)

lemma[fact] L59:gideon-had-documented-opportunity-type-ruth-likely-estate "Gideon had a documented opportunity to type Ruth's likely estate-office summons shortly before it was filed, while Felix was at Vesper House; opportunity and machine access do not alone prove authorship."
  <- AND#J60(P123, P199, P203, L29)

lemma[fact] L60:gideon-had-access-old-march-rowe-labels-thorn "Gideon had access to old March & Rowe labels and the Thorn plans and was alone in the estate office immediately before the carrier collected Aldous's parcel, while Felix was documented elsewhere; these facts establish a strong preparation opportunity but are not a direct eyewitness account."
  <- AND#J61(P72, P77, P108, P192, P200, P201, P202, P203)

lemma[fact] L61:ruth-was-deliberately-lured-under-aldous-initials-killed "Ruth was deliberately lured under Aldous's initials and killed after a struggle by being forcefully put into the path of a freight wagon; the evidence does not establish every movement in the struggle."
  <- AND#J62(P117, P124, P127, P128, P204, P205, L31)

lemma[fact] L62:aldous-collapse-probably-drove-chair-into-desk-whose "Aldous's collapse probably drove the chair into the desk, whose sideways jolt bent the clock's balance staff and stopped it; if Wren's twelve-minute comparison was accurate, this occurred at approximately 9:39."
  <- AND#J63(P44, P94, P206, P207, P208, P209)

lemma[fact] L63:confirmed-aconitine-poisoning-compatible-aldous-speaking-9-18 "Confirmed aconitine poisoning is compatible with Aldous speaking at 9:18 because puncture-delivered aconitine can leave a victim able to speak for several minutes; this does not independently authenticate the voice or fix the puncture time."
  <- AND#J64(P29, P55, P185)

lemma[fact] L64:gideon-billiards-alibi-covers-probable-delayed-fatal-collapse "Gideon's billiards alibi covers the probable delayed fatal collapse, not the earlier acquisition of poison, construction of the mechanism, or preparation of the parcel, so it does not establish innocence."
  <- AND#J65(P210, P211, P212, L21)

lemma[fact] L65:row-not-account-ruth-meant-that-her-notebook "By 'the row, not the account,' Ruth meant that her notebook's number 17 referred to collection Row 17 and the false Vesper Psalter, whereas her opponent had mistaken it for the secret Escrow 17 account."
  <- AND#J66(P126, P133, L42, L58)

lemma[fact] L66:aldous-connected-ruth-row-17-investigation-escrow-17 "Aldous connected Ruth's Row 17 investigation to Escrow 17 by recognizing the two-number confusion: Ruth's note and spoken correction concerned the collection row, while the fragment he carried came from the account statement; his unfinished sentence records that inference without preserving its final words."
  <- AND#J67(P49, P126, P133, P155, P173, P177, L36, L42)

lemma[fact] L67:complete-circumstantial-intersection-identifies-gideon-ruth-killer-he "The complete circumstantial intersection identifies Gideon as Ruth's killer: he had the concealed-account motive and unique shown knowledge, encountered her open Row 17 notebook, had the opportunity to type the false summons, and the later injuries establish a deliberate freight-yard killing."
  <- AND#J68(L45, L46, L58, L59, L61)

lemma[fact] L68:gideon-lured-ruth-parcels-office-under-aldous-initials "Gideon lured Ruth to the parcels office under Aldous's initials because he mistook her Row 17 investigation for discovery of Escrow 17; after she corrected him during their confrontation, a struggle ended with Gideon forcefully putting her into the moving wagon's path, most likely to silence her and conceal his own conduct."
  <- AND#J69(P117, P124, P126, P204, L58, L61, L67)

lemma[fact] L69:escrow-17-was-false-account-it-disguised-unsupported "Escrow 17 was the false account: it disguised unsupported payments through a defunct bookseller and bearer drafts; Gideon administered it, although the bank records do not independently trace the ultimate recipient."
  <- AND#J70(P155, P167, P169, L45, L47)

lemma[fact] L70:full-intersection-identifies-gideon-aldous-killer-exposure-escrow "The full intersection identifies Gideon as Aldous's killer: exposure of Escrow 17 supplied motive, March & Rowe and the office supplied the parcel disguise and preparation opportunity, the unreturned key supplied poison access, the Thorn plans supplied the mechanism, and the delayed collapse made his billiards alibi compatible with guilt."
  <- AND#J71(L47, L50, L56, L57, L60, L64, P213)

lemma[fact] L71:best-supported-reconstruction-that-gideon-built-hollow-spine "The best-supported reconstruction is that Gideon built the hollow-spine Thorn mechanism, coated its retracting needle with aconitine and marking dye, packed it under an obsolete March & Rowe label, and sent it to Aldous; Aldous activated it himself by pressing the clasp inside the already locked study."
  <- AND#J72(L53, L54, L55, L56, L60, L70)

lemma[fact] L72:vesper-psalter-facsimile-was-aldous-false-collection-object "The Vesper Psalter facsimile was Aldous's false collection object, while 'A Dissertation Concerning the Tides' was a newly constructed murder-device disguise rather than the false object he had promised to expose."
  <- AND#J73(P154, L43, L55)

lemma[fact] L73:no-voice-imitation-supernatural-event-live-illusion-needed "No voice imitation, supernatural event, or live illusion is needed for the locked room: the clasp delivered a delayed poison and retracted its needle, allowing Aldous to speak before later dying alone."
  <- AND#J74(P55, P183, L54, L63)

lemma[fact] L74:completed-solution-that-beatrice-created-false-vesper-psalter "The completed solution is that Beatrice created the false Vesper Psalter, Escrow 17 was the false account, and Gideon killed both Ruth and Aldous to protect the concealed-account scheme and prevent its exposure."
  <- AND#J75(L43, L69, L67, L68, L70)
